{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Come on the [G]sloop John B.,
My grandfather and [D7]me,
Round Nassau town we did [G]roam;
Drinking all [G7]night, we got in a [C]fight,
I feel so [G]break-up, [D7]I want to go [G]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
So [G]hoist up the John B. sails,
See how the mainsail [D7]set,
Send for the captain ashore, let me go [G]home;
[G7]Let me go home, let me go [C]home,
I feel so [G]break-up, [D7]I want to go [G]home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
The [G]first mate he got drunk,
Break up the people's [D7]trunk,
Constable come aboard and take him a[G]way;
Sheriff [G7]Johnstone, please let me a[C]lone,
I feel so [G]break-up, [D7]I want to go [G]home.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: The traditional Bahamian words, not the 1966 pop arrangement.}
{x_end: G}
